# Every text file is UTF-8 without a BOM and ends its lines with LF, on every platform, Windows
# checkouts included: eol overrides a contributor's core.autocrlf. .editorconfig asks editors
# for the same, and .github/scripts/tests/test_text_files.py fails CI on a CR, a BOM or a file
# that is not UTF-8. Binary extensions are named below so that no heuristic decides it.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.a     binary
*.lib   binary
*.dll   binary
*.so    binary
*.dylib binary
*.jar   binary
*.png   binary

# What a `git archive` of this repository leaves out. PIE (the PHP extension installer) reads
# the Composer package from Packagist, which serves GitHub's archive of the tag, and takes
# only its metadata from it: the extension itself is a pre-packaged binary attached to the
# release. So the archive carries composer.json, LICENSE, README.md and go/, nothing else,
# and `test_git_archive_is_metadata_only` pins that set.
#
# A deny-list on purpose, and `go/` is deliberately not on it: the Go module proxy builds
# the module zip with `git archive` of that directory, so an export-ignore that reached it
# would publish an empty or partial Go module. A new top-level path that is not listed
# here only costs download size, and that test fails until it is listed. SwiftPM clones,
# and every other registry gets a built package, so nothing else reads these attributes.
# They apply from the tree being archived: a tag made before this file existed keeps its
# full archive.
/.claude           export-ignore
/.editorconfig     export-ignore
/.gitattributes    export-ignore
/.github           export-ignore
/.gitignore        export-ignore
/CHANGELOG.md      export-ignore
/CLAUDE.md         export-ignore
/CRAN_CHECKLIST.md export-ignore
/global.json       export-ignore
/Package.swift     export-ignore
/ROADMAP.md        export-ignore
/c                 export-ignore
/corpus            export-ignore
/csharp            export-ignore
/docs              export-ignore
/include           export-ignore
/java              export-ignore
/php               export-ignore
/python            export-ignore
/r                 export-ignore
/ruby              export-ignore
/rust              export-ignore
/swift             export-ignore
/typescript        export-ignore
